.TH BANDHOP 1 "October 2026" "Bandhop 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bandhop \- terminal-first internet radio controller for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bandhop
.I COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bandhop is a Rust internet radio player that manages stations from a local configuration file and delegates audio playback to mpv. A per-user foreground session or optional systemd service receives commands on a private Unix socket. Playback never starts automatically on daemon startup.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create a default empty station configuration.
.TP
.B listen
Run a foreground interactive session (p=toggle, n=next, s=status, q=quit, each followed by Enter).
.TP
.B daemon
Run the control daemon (suitable for a systemd user service).
.TP
.B play | stop | toggle | next | status
Control a running Bandhop instance. Next advances circularly and does not start a stopped player.
.TP
.B stations list | add NAME URL | remove ID | move ID POSITION
Manage the ordered channel library.
.TP
.B config path | show | edit | validate | reload
Manage the configuration.
.TP
.B service install | enable | disable | status | uninstall
Manage the optional systemd user service.
.TP
.B keys show | check | setup
Print and inspect KDE Plasma shortcut setup instructions. F13 toggles; F14 advances to the next station.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/bandhop/config.toml
Station configuration (respecting XDG_CONFIG_HOME).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/bandhop/state
Selected station ID (respecting XDG_STATE_HOME).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bandhop-runtime/control.sock
Local control socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.SH LICENSE
MIT OR Apache-2.0

.SH NOTIFICATIONS
.TP
.B bandhop notify test
Send a normal-urgency test notification through the active daemon. KDE Plasma controls popup visibility.
